1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,442
The fifth arc closed at a bridge, not at a station.

2
00:00:03,442 --> 00:00:15,963
A formal presentation had been drafted for the church hall in the north, and a second one for the south; a cable, a sign, and a badge on the table were all the gear they had.

3
00:00:15,963 --> 00:00:22,931
“The medium is the trip,” Aisha said, “and the trip is the document.”

4
00:00:22,931 --> 00:00:35,892
The mission had become an associate: a small organization for the protection of passengers, with a guest list, a reservation book, and a seat for every complaint.

5
00:00:35,892 --> 00:00:43,229
“You cannot explain a bridge to someone who has never bent under a load,” the old cowboy said.

6
00:00:43,229 --> 00:00:50,942
His only hobby was the railway, and his heel had worn a trace in the aisle of the carriage.

7
00:00:50,942 --> 00:01:00,989
What happened next was a migration of habits rather than of people: the cruise passengers learned the ferry, and the commuters learned the shuttle.

8
00:01:00,989 --> 00:01:05,588
“We leave nothing behind but a log,” Maya said.

9
00:01:05,588 --> 00:01:13,116
“And a log is a way of saying: we were here, in the night, at this window.”

10
00:01:13,116 --> 00:01:16,300
The repair of the cabin took a week.

11
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:27,611
A swallow nested under the bay window, a tender note arrived from the associate in the country, and a draft of the new timetable was pinned to the aisle wall.

12
00:01:27,611 --> 00:01:31,745
“We receive more than we create,” Lin wrote.

13
00:01:31,745 --> 00:01:35,639
“That is why the position matters.”

14
00:01:35,639 --> 00:01:47,950
Around the bridge, the town had begun to endure its own success: a trail for tourists, a rest stop, and a forward step that nobody had planned.

15
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:55,723
“About a year from now,” the associate said, “somebody will say we did it like that on purpose.

16
00:01:55,723 --> 00:02:06,770
We must explain what really happened.” It was, in the end, the same promise as before, moved one bridge further along.

17
00:02:06,770 --> 00:02:19,366
The church by the bay had a god in its window and a finish to its stone that no repair could copy; the aisle, the seat, and the tender farewell were all part of the same formal goodbye.

18
00:02:19,366 --> 00:02:24,435
The mission was finished, and the associate would keep the log.

19
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:29,478
A hobby became a badge, and a badge became a promise.

20
00:02:29,478 --> 00:02:41,245
A gender balance in the crew, a transit pass for every guest, and a plan to initiate a second trail: these were the last three items on the draft.

21
00:02:41,245 --> 00:02:49,646
A border is not a line on the ground; it is the distance between what you meant and what arrived.
